1 0 0 1 48 716 Tm (Educational use only. Not legal advice. Verify against your CC&Rs and state law.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 703 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 48 690 Tm (== VISUAL SUMMARY ==) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 677 Tm (Five takeaways to remember about when mediation beats hearings or court. Use them as a) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 664 Tm (one-page briefing before you write or speak.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 651 Tm (* Start with procedure: Map notice, cure, hearing, and decision duties before debating the aesthetics of when mediation beats hearings or court.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 638 Tm (* Make the decision point explicit: Your appeal should answer whether ADR is available and useful now with exhibits, not adjectives.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 625 Tm (* Compare options deliberately: Know whether you are closer to Documented ADR clause, Voluntary mediation, or ADR not available before you escalate.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 612 Tm (* Write one remedy sentence: Boards skim-state waive, reduce, re-notice, or reverse in a single line tied to when mediation beats hearings or court.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 599 Tm (* Keep escalation proportionate: Match collections risk and dollar amount to mediation, counsel, or court only after the packet is complete.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 586 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 48 573 Tm (== PROCESS FLOW ==) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 560 Tm (1. Capture the trigger [Same day \(30-90 min\)]) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 547 Tm (Save the notice, portal message, invoice, or verbal summary that started the dispute about) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 534 Tm (when mediation beats hearings or court. Note the date received.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 521 Tm (   Documents: Violation notice, invoice, or portal message; Envelope postmark or delivery receipt; Dated note of when you first learned of the issue) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 508 Tm (   Avoid: Relying on a verbal warning without a written artifact; Forgetting to photograph the notice date and cited rule) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 495 Tm (2. Pull controlling text [1-3 days]) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 482 Tm (Locate the statute, CC&R, rule, and fine-schedule language that supposedly authorizes action) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 469 Tm (on when mediation beats hearings or court.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 456 Tm (   Documents: CC&R / rule pages cited in the notice; Current fine schedule; Bylaws appeal or hearing clause) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 443 Tm (   Avoid: Arguing fairness before confirming the board cited a real rule; Using an outdated schedule that no longer matches the ledger) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 430 Tm (3. Build the evidence spine [2-5 days]) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 417 Tm (Assemble dated photos, correspondence, ledgers, and comparables that speak directly to) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 404 Tm (whether ADR is available and useful now.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 391 Tm (   Documents: Dated photos or maintenance logs; Correspondence export; Comparable-neighbor notes \(when relevant\); One-page exhibit index) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 378 Tm (   Avoid: Photos without dates, landmarks, or consistent angles; Dumping unsorted emails instead of labeled exhibits) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 365 Tm (4. Choose the procedural path [Per notice window \(often 7-14 days\)]) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 352 Tm (Pick cure, informal dispute, formal hearing, payment under protest, ADR, or counsel based on) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 339 Tm (deadlines and stakes around when mediation beats hearings or court.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 326 Tm (   Documents: Deadline calendar from the notice and bylaws; Draft remedy sentence \(waive / reduce / re-notice / reverse\); Proof of any cure already completed) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 313 Tm (   Avoid: Missing the internal appeal deadline while still gathering evidence; Asking for conflicting remedies in the same letter) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 300 Tm (5. Submit a written ask [1-2 hours to finalize + send]) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 287 Tm (Send one clear remedy request \(waive, reduce, re-notice, or reverse\) tied to whether ADR is) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 274 Tm (available and useful now, with exhibits attached.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 261 Tm (   Documents: Signed appeal or dispute letter; Indexed exhibits; Certified-mail / portal delivery proof) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 248 Tm (   Avoid: Sending exhibits without a clear ask on the first page; Failing to keep delivery proof for the appeal packet) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 235 Tm (6. Confirm the outcome in writing [1-7 days after hearing or board action]) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 222 Tm (Demand or calendar a written decision, update your ledger notes, and decide whether) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 209 Tm (escalation is still proportionate.) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 196 Tm (   Documents: Written decision or refusal-to-decide record; Updated ledger screenshot; Post-decision deadline calendar) Tj
1 0 0 1 48 183 Tm (   Avoid: Assuming silence means the fine was waived; Paying without noting payment under protest when escalation continues) Tj
